MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Aenima feels like the clearest next choice after 10.000 Days because I want more of Tool's intricate rhythms and dark atmosphere; Year Zero also fits that atmospheric, heavy mood.",
    "Mutter, City of Evil, and Vol. 3 appeal because they combine forceful riffs with melody, connecting with my interest in In Flames, Advance And Vanquish, and Ten Thousand Fists."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Stadium Arcadium's funk-oriented rock and Agaetis Byrjun's gentler atmosphere do not satisfy my current desire for heavy, forceful music.",
    "Extreme Aggression fits my heavier interests, but aggression alone is not enough today; I am more drawn to melody and atmosphere. No. 4 fits broadly but feels less compelling than another Tool album."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My rock listening seems to have been treated as a broad preference, even though funk-oriented rock does not match what I want right now.",
    "My heavier albums seem to suggest that any aggressive music will appeal equally, but I distinguish between sheer intensity and heaviness balanced with melody."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent interaction with 10.000 Days makes Tool's particular combination of rhythmic complexity and dark atmosphere especially relevant now.",
    "An album can fit my taste without being something I would choose today: I would prioritize Aenima over No. 4 and try Vol. 3 before the presumed All Hope Is Gone."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations captured my interest in heavy music but sometimes missed the melody, rhythmic complexity, and dark atmosphere that make a choice compelling right now."
}
